{{Quote|"An Omnitrix?!"<br>"THE Omnitrix. An improved version I've been working on ever since you were given the [[Omnitrix (Original)|prototype]] [[And Then There Were 10|six years ago.]]"|[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]].<ref name="TUE2">''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]''</ref>}}
The '''Omnitrix''' is the device that '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Ben 10: Omniverse]]''' revolved around. It is the finished version of the original [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]].

==Appearance==
The Omnitrix resembles a digital wristwatch. Its faceplate is now square rather than round and has a white, green, and black color scheme. The faceplate is black with two green stripes forming an outline for the hourglass of the Galvan tech logo. When the faceplate is slid back, the Omnitrix's core is revealed, resembling the original Omnitrix's faceplate. When selecting an alien, a holographic circle floats and rotates to allow the user to select an alien.

===Original Future Timeline===
The Omnitrix in the [[Original Future Timeline]] looks almost identical, with the only difference being that the side stripes are colored black instead of green.

<gallery hideaddbutton="true" bordercolor="transparent" captionalign="center" spacing="small">
OV Omnitrix replica.png|The Omnitrix in the [[Original Future Timeline]]
</gallery>

==History ==
===Background===
According to Azmuth, he started working on this Omnitrix ever since [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] got the [[Omnitrix (Original)|prototype]] during the events of ''[[And Then There Were 10]]''. He has spent approximately six years constructing it.

===Ultimate Alien===
This Omnitrix was first mentioned by Azmuth in ''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''. He was planning on giving it to Ben, but stated that it was not complete. He also mentioned that Ben's maturity needed to increase before he would be allowed to use it.

Towards the end of '''Ultimate Alien''', Azmuth had completed this Omnitrix. In ''[[The Ultimate Enemy: Part 2]]'', Azmuth finally gave it to Ben because he deemed him worthy of wielding it shortly after removing the Ultimatrix from the latter's wrist. When Ben asked Azmuth if he would give him the Master Control, Azmuth stated he would likely activate the Master Control on his 18th birthday. 

Ben has worn this Omnitrix ever since.  

===Omniverse ===
In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] temporarily wore the Omnitrix after Ben Prime was erased from existence by the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]].

In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', No Watch Ben returned the Omnitrix to Ben Prime after the latter was restored by the former as [[Clockwork]] alongside all of his other counterparts.

===[[Original Future Timeline]]===
Many years later, [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben]] gave the Omnitrix to his son, [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]]. However, Ken went on a mission he was not allowed to go on at some point after this, and got in over his head, prompting Ben to take his Omnitrix from him.{{Refn|[[:File:Why Ken Lost His Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}}

In ''[[The End of an Era]]'', Ken is shown handing over the Omnitrix to his [[Kai Tennyson|mother]] when it is brought up.

