==Modes==
<tabber>
|-|Active=[[File:Omniverseomnitrixactive.png|thumb|200px|left|Active Mode]]
Active Mode is the Omnitrix's default mode when idle. In this mode, the user can select the transformation they want to become; initiate the process of transforming; and stay in said transformation for 15 minutes at a time.<ref>''[[Hot Stretch]]''</ref> However, different factors and actions performed by the user can severely diminish the available usage time: most commonly if the user, while transformed, changes to another form.{{Refn|https://archive.md/A42xJ|group = MW|name = Archive1}} If the user slams the core, this can affect the time limit of a transformation,<ref name="Azmuth" /><ref name="FaFBM">''[[For a Few Brains More]]''</ref> as the user could stay transformed for hours.<ref>''[[No Honor Among Bros]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[:File:NHAB Extended Time Limit.png]]|group = DJW}}

|-|Recharge=[[File:DepreyPresa1P309.png|thumb|200px|left|Recharge Mode]]
When the Omnitrix's usage time is fully depleted (i.e. "times out"), it goes into Recharge Mode: firstly warning of the timing out; then detransforming the user and locking all functions of Active Mode while the Omnitrix recharges.
[[File:AND (223).png|thumb|200px|right|Time Out]]
The Omnitrix is capable of detecting when it's host is in any sort of life-threatening distress. Specifically, it can instantly recharge to protect the user from a direct physical threat. This was shown when Ben was instantly turned into [[Feedback]] to contain the energy of [[Maltruant]]'s [[Annihilarrgh]].<ref name="AND">''[[A New Dawn]]''</ref>

If the user is knocked out or hurt enough, the Omnitrix will revert them to their normal form.

|-|Collect/Capture=[[File:TVSB51.PNG|thumb|200px|left|Collect Mode]]
When a new DNA sample has been unlocked,<ref>''[[Outbreak]]''</ref> or when the Omnitrix captures new DNA not present in the catalog,<ref name = TVSB>''[[The Vampire Strikes Back]]''</ref>  Collect Mode is activated. However, if the Omnitrix is far away from the detected sample, the Omnitrix's other functions will be disabled until the alien is scanned.<ref name = TVSB/>
[[File:OB (663).png|200px|right|The Omnitrix symbol shooting green ray]]
When in alien form, the Omnitrix shoots out a green ray from the dial.

It scans to match the species, then moves the identified species to the active playlist. If it seen the species before, it does it passively, without Ben actively scanning.<ref name = TVSB/>

When the Omnitrix scans the DNA of an alien it doesn't have, it won't always be immediately unlocked in the arsenal.{{Refn|[[:File:When the Omnitrix scans new DNA.png]]|group = DJW}}

|-|Self-Destruct=[[File:IaMBW2 (430).png|thumb|200px|right|Self-Destruct]]
The Omnitrix has a self-destruction mode. In this mode, the Omnitrix will begin a countdown, beeping as a warning that the mode has been activated. It can be enabled if settings are changed, and can be disabled if settings are changed again.<ref>''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]''</ref>{{Refn|[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] states that the Omnitrix does not have a self-destruction mode, and that Ben has never encountered one.{{Refn|[[:File:No Self Destruction in OV Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}} This however is against the ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'' episode.{{Refn|[[Ben 10 Planet:Policies/Canon Hierarchy|Canon Hierarchy]]|group = BTP|name = hierarchy}}|group = note}}

|-|Randomizer=[[File:TFoW1 (83).png|thumb|200px|right|Randomizer]]
The Omnitrix has a randomizer function that works in one of two ways: either the user will continuously change between different aliens every few minutes before timing out, or they will turn into one random alien for an inconsistently short period of time before changing back.<ref name="TFoW1" />
</tabber>

