*If the Omnitrix does mis-transform, it is because of the user slamming on the Omnitrix's core{{Refn|http://archive.is/qBK7L|group = DJW}} too hard and (inadvertently) the scroll pad.{{Refn|Azmuth warned Ben not to bang so hard on the Omnitrix core when transforming, as the impact will send the timeout function to a random selection.<ref name="FaFBM"/> This is considered the main on-screen reason why Ben often did not get the alien form he wanted. However, in ''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]'' and a ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', Ben wanted to turn into [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] and [[XLR8 (Classic)|XLR8]], selected Humungousaur and turned into [[Waterhazard]] and [[Clockwork]] in both the aforementioned episodes.|group = note}}
*Much like the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|original Ultimatrix]],<ref>''[[Inspector 13]]''</ref> the Omnitrix is not hack proof.{{Refn|http://archive.is/fSpWt|group = DJW}}
*Like the previous models,<ref>'''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''</ref><ref name="TUE2" /> the Omnitrix does not have a failsafe against [[Magic (Classic)|magic]].{{Refn|[[:File:No Failsafes Against Magic.png]]|group = DJW}} 
**If the Omnitrix symbol is bitten by magic creatures, such as [[Rock Monster|rock monsters]], the device will send a shockwave, detransform the user and will select only one alien.<ref name="MI" />
*Like the original Omnitrix, any occasional damage the user sustains is retained when said user times out.
*The DNA Scanner of the Omnitrix will attempt to scan any new DNA in the vicinity. If the DNA sample is too far away, then the Omnitrix will shut down all its other functions until it scans the new sample.<ref name="TVSB" />
*The user can be prevented from transforming by the [[Forever Knights]] [[DNA Scanner]] which would scan the transformations' DNA before reverting the user.<ref name="RtF">''[[Return to Forever]]''</ref> 
* Too many transformations and reversals will wear out the Omnitrix, causing it to go into a cooldown cycle.<ref name="RtF" />
*The Omnitrix has no mind control protection.<ref>''[[Catfight]]''</ref>
*The Omnitrix may stop working when frozen in time by a [[Chronosapien]].<ref name="MM" />
*The Omnitrix communicator does not connect to the [[Null Void (Classic)|Null Void]].<ref>''[[The Most Dangerous Game Show]]''</ref>
*Upon activating the Randomizer Function, the user will constantly switch transformations at the most inopportune times, thereby putting them into potentially dangerous situations.<ref name="TFoW1">''[[The Frogs of War: Part 1]]''</ref> 
*When exposed to electromagnetic interference from beings like [[Phil Billings (Classic)|Phil]], it can make the Omnitrix transform the user into electrical aliens even when they select a different alien.<ref>''[[Max's Monster]]''</ref>
*Due to a programming error, Rath had been running around naked for most of the series, until [[Skurd]] corrected the error and gave Rath a Luchador costume.<ref name="STDS" />{{Refn|[[:File:Rath Clothed Permanent.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Rath Clothed Permanent 2.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The genetics of some species can alter the user's personality, as it occurs with [[Rath (Classic)|Rath]].{{Refn|[[:File:Aliens' genetics affect Ben's personality.png]]|group = CM}}
*If tampered with by Temporal interference such as from [[Eon]], the Omnitrix can transfer the user's mind in cross-time to a younger version.<ref name="BA">''[[Ben Again]]''</ref>
*The Omnitrix is vulnerable to devices that operate at a sub-quantum level that can destroy it, such as the [[Non-Baryonic Disruptor Chamber]].<ref>[[Alan Albright]]</ref><ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>
*The Omnitrix disconnects from the user if the user is de-aged, requiring the use of other recognition methods to reconnect with the user.<ref>''[[Arrested Development]]''</ref>
*The anti-death failsafe is limited and can allow the user to die depending on the circumstances.<ref>''[[And Then There Were None]]''</ref>

