==Trivia== 
*Unlike the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]] and the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]], the Omnitrix has a digitalized feminine voice, rather than the digitalized version of Ben's voice.
*In addition to the ones listed above, the Omnitrix has hundreds of other features Ben does not know about.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Other Features.png]]|group = DJW}} For example, he does not know how to access the settings that changes the user's gender to adapt to another species.{{Refn|group = DJW|name = gender}}
**[[Derrick J. Wyatt|Derrick]] believed that the Omnitrix has all the features of the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original]].{{Refn|[[:File:OV Omnitrix has all the features of the original.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Unlike the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]], the Omnitrix does not have an evolutionary feature.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Omnitrix No Evolutionary Function.png]]|group = DJW}} Also, a [[Polymorphic Crystal]] cannot transform the Omnitrix itself into an Ultimatrix.{{Refn|[[:File:Polymorphic Crystal Will Not Turn Omnitrix Into Ultimatrix.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Because of these factors, Ben will never regain the ability to transform into [[Ultimate Forms]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Will Never Regain Ultimate Forms.png]]|group = DJW}}
*It is implied that aliens such as [[Astrodactyl]], [[Ball Weevil]], [[Bloxx (Classic)|Bloxx]], [[Crashhopper]], [[Gutrot]], and [[Toepick]] were never locked in the Omnitrix.{{Refn|[[:File:New Aliens in OV Weren't Locked.png]]|group = DJW}}  
**In regard to [[Gravattack]], it is implied that he was unlocked sometime before ''[[Double or Nothing]]''. This is because Albedo is able to transform into Negative Gravattack, and his powers only allow him to turn into all the aliens Ben has unlocked prior to that episode, though Derrick later stated he was wrong about said claim due to Negative Gravattack.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Retracted Double or Nothing Statement.png]]|group=DJW}}
**In regard to [[Feedback]], [[Matt Youngberg]], [[Derrick J. Wyatt]], and [[Kevin Rubio]] believe that Ben reabsorbed Feedback's DNA when he was floating inside Malware because Malware absorbed both the transformation and a little bit of Ben's genetic code when he destroyed Feedback. Thus, part of him really was missing.{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin Rubio's Explanation on Feedback.png]]|group = KR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Youngberg's Explanation on Feedback 2.png]]|group = MY}}{{Refn|[[:File:Malware Absorbed Feedback's Genetic Fragments.png]]|group = DJW}}
*During '''Omniverse'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s early run, [[Matt Wayne]] believed that [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] had not unlocked [[Spitter]] as of ''[[The Frogs of War: Part 2]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Spitter Not Unlocked in OV.png]]|group = MW}} Later during the show's run, Derrick stated that Spitter was unlocked off-screen after '''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]''''' and is available to Ben in present day.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Spitter Unlocked During Flashbacks.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
**Correlating with this, when asked if [[Benzarro]] has access to Spitter, Derrick stated "It seems like he has access to most of what Ben does".{{Refn|[[:File:Benzarro Spitter.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*The Omnitrix contains interdimensional white lab mouse DNA, though Ben is not aware of this.{{Refn|http://archive.is/D1Ss9|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Is Unaware of White Lab Mouse DNA.png]]|group = DJW}}      
**The Omnitrix also contains dolphin DNA.{{Refn|[[:File:Dolphin DNA in Omnitrix Proof.png]]|group = DJW}}
**This is a reference to ''The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy'', a book series by Douglas Adams. In the series, it is mentioned humanity is the third most intelligent species on Earth, behind white mice and dolphins.
*[[Unitaur]] and [[Slapstrike]] are not actual aliens/transformations and were created just for '''[[The Ben Ten Show]]''' (although not by Deefus himself).{{Refn|[[:File:Slapstrike and Unitaur Fake.png]]|group = DJW}}
*When explaining why he was unable to turn into [[Juryrigg]], [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] states that he turned into aliens "he never knew he had" before eventually turning into [[Eatle]] off-screen prior to the chronological start of the episode ''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''.
**[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] once stated that the unproduced alien [[Ventrilosquid]] was one of those aliens.{{Refn|[[:File:Ventrilosquid LDTTWA.PNG]]|group = DJW}} However, years later, he stated that he was joking.{{Refn|[[:File:Ventrilosquid LDTTWA Joke.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Derrick believed that non-canon aliens [[Rocks]] and [[Squidstrictor]] are available in the Omnitrix,{{Refn|[[:File:Rocks and Squidstrictor Canon.png]]|group = DJW}} having been unlocked off-screen prior to ''[[The More Things Change: Part 1]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Rocks and Squidstrictor Unlocked Before OV.png]]|group = DJW}} This is because he wanted to incorporate those aliens into the show before the network intervened.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick Wanted to Add Rocks and Squidstrictor Into OV.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Scrapped Omnitrix transformations conceptualized by Derrick prior to working on '''Omniverse''' were that of an unnamed stretchy alien likened to [[wikipedia:Mister Fantastic|Mister Fantastic]] that was shaped like a flatworm,{{Refn|[[:File:Stretchy Alien like a Flatworm.png]]|group=DJW}} a six-legged alien likened to [[w:c:hanna-barbera:Tundro|Tundro]] from '''[[wikipedia:The Herculoids|The Herculoids]]''', and a "golem-stone [[wikipedia:Frankenstein's monster|Frankenstein]]".{{Refn|[[:File:Turd Burglar Proof.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*The crew came up with a bunch of names for aliens available to Ben at age 16, including The Zilch, Pyxl-Loaf, Crocduster, Overround, The Sledge, Splatterator, Dropsies, Tranquenstine, Tanker Bell (named after Senator Howell Tankerbell from '''[[Wikipedia:Mr. Show with Bob and David|Mr. Show with Bob and David]]'''),{{Refn|[[:File:Tanker Bell Etymology.png]]|group = DJW}} Mister Sister, THUUG, The Walking Dread, Polywhirl, Tool Bucket, Murphybed, Turdberry, and Brundlefoot.{{Refn|[[:File:DJW Joke Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Ben 23 Joke Aliens.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|https://ask.fm/DerrickJWyatt/answers/121382560884|group = DJW}}  
**Mister Sister is inspired by [https://mazinger.fandom.com/wiki/Baron_Ashura/TV Baron Ashura] from [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mazinger_Z Mazinger Z] and would have had a split personality.{{Refn|[[:File:Mister Sister is based on Baron Ashura.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Mister Sister has a split personality.png]]|group = DJW}} 
**Pyxl-Loaf would have had pixel and bread-related powers.{{Refn|[[:File:Pyxl Loaf Powers.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Crocduster swoops over people and gasses them.{{Refn|[[:File:Crocduster Powers.png]]|group = DJW}}
*There were technical glitches in the original Omnitrix and Ultimatrix that limited the positioning of the symbol during transformations that caused interferences such as unclothed appearances. Azmuth reformatted and corrected these errors in the current Omnitrix.{{Refn|[[:File:Old Omnitrix Glitches.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The Omnitrix is always receiving software updates from [[Galvan Prime (Classic)|Galvan Prime]].{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Software Updates.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The Omnitrix is unable to scan and accept the DNA of certain beings and species including the Ultimate Forms,{{Refn|''link unavailable''|group = DJW}} cybernetically-enhanced beings,{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Dalek & Cybermen DNA.png]]|group = DJW}} mutants such as [[Osmosian]]s,{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Cannot Accept Mutant DNA.png]]|group = DJW}} living spaceships depicted as commonplace objects,{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Cannot Accept TARDIS DNA.png]]|group = DJW}} and non-sapient races that do not have as much sentience as [[Nemetrix]] predators. 
**It neither contains nor accepts DNA from species such as [[Slime-Biot]]s and [[Contumelia]] because neither of them have genetic material equivalent enough to traditional DNA that can be stored.{{Refn|[[:File:No Slimebiote DNA In Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:No Contumelia DNA In Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Derrick believed that the Omnitrix cannot accept [[Cryptid (Classic)|cryptid]] DNA,{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Cannot Accept Cryptid DNA.png]]|group = DJW}} but Matt Wayne says it may be possible.{{Refn|[[:File:Buzzshock Must Learn To Duplicate.png]]|group = MW}}
**When asked if it can accept [[w:c:steven-universe:Gems|Gem]] DNA, Derrick answered "not in [his] show".{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Gem DNA.png]]|group = DJW}} This implies that the acceptance of such DNA is a case depending on the writer.
*The Omnitrix is unable to accommodate the DNA of magical creatures such as [[Rock Monster]]s and other inhabitants of [[Legerdomain]] because magic is not compatible with the science of the Omnitrix.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Cannot Accomodate Magical Creatures.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Cannot Accept Stone Creature DNA.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Azmuth can lock the Omnitrix in person and remotely,{{Refn|[[:File:Azmuth Can Lock the OV Omnitrix.png]]|group = MW}} much like what he did with the [[Ultimatrix (Stabilizer)|recreated Ultimatrix]].<ref>''[[Malgax Attacks]]''</ref>
*[[Charlotte McDuffie]] believes the Omnitrix is immune to [[Magic (Classic)|Magic]].{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix is immune to Magic.png]]|group = CM}}
*When asked what kind of enhancement he could imagine for the Omnitrix, Derrick responded that he would add a space/environmental suit that could be accessed when needed.{{Refn|[[:File:Derrick's Omnitrix Improvement Idea.png]]|group = DJW}}
**This idea is similar to the [[Omni-Naut Armors]] from the [[Dimension 27998.3|'''Reboot''' Continuity]].
*Derrick always believed that the Omnitrix transformed the user into the apex version of their respective species, almost like like that species' superhero.{{Refn|[[:File:Prime Specimen Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW|name = apex}}
**However, [[Dwayne McDuffie|Dwayne]] considered the transformations to be common members of the species,{{Refn|group = DJW|name = apex}} with [[Duncan Rouleau|Duncan]] agreeing, stating that the Omnitrix transforms the user into fully functional versions of the species.{{Refn|[[:File:Duncan's Opinion on Optimized Adults.png]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Transforms the User into Functional Versions.png]]|group = DR}}
**[[Charlotte McDuffie|Charlotte]] never thought of the transformations as being the apex of their species, just examples.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix aliens are not apex species.png]]|group = CM}}
**[[Matt Wayne|Matt]] stated that the Omnitrix transforms the user into genetically optimized adults of their respective species.{{Refn|[[:File:Omnitrix Aliens are Optimized Adults.png]]|group = MW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Nemetrix Damaging.PNG]]|group = MW}}
***However, the way age affects the Omnitrix's transformations has been inconsistently represented throughout the series, so this may not always be correct.
*Unlike some of Ben's alternate counterparts, [[Eon]]'s Omnitrix did not have a unique name.{{Refn|[[:File:Eon's Omnitrix Does Not Have A Special Name.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The Omnitrix was designed by [[Matt Youngberg]] and Shane Poindexter{{Refn|[[:File:Matt and Shane designed the new Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}} under the former's supervision. Matt had a really clear vision of what he wanted, and Derrick liked the direction they were going.{{Refn|[[:File:Direction With New Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}}   
**For its brief appearance in '''Ultimate Alien''', it was designed by [[Norm Ryang]] based off Youngberg's concepts.{{Refn|[[:File:Norm Ryang Designed OV Omnitrix.png]]|group = DJW}}
*The Omnitrix's touch screen interface and Randomizer function were both Youngberg's ideas.{{Refn|http://archive.is/dM5U5|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[:File:Matt Youngberg Randomizer.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*The alien icons on the touch screen interface were designed by TJ Collins{{Refn|[[:File:TJ Collins Omnitrix Icons.png]]|group = DJW}} and are inspired by the Autobot and Decepticon insignias from ''Transformers: Animated'', another Cartoon Network animated series that Wyatt had worked on.{{Refn|http://archive.is/Qe5w7|group = DJW}}

